# Direct backend dependencies — the only file edited by hand.
#
# requirements.txt next to it is generated from this one and pins EVERY package,
# transitive ones included. Pinning only what is listed here is not enough: a
# scaffolded app once stopped booting with `No module named 'psycopg'` because
# flask-sqlalchemy pulled SQLAlchemy unpinned and 2.1 changed what a bare
# `postgresql://` URL means. Twenty-six packages were floating like that.
#
# Python 3.10 is the floor: the lock is resolved for it, and the pins it produces
# were checked to install on 3.12 (what the image runs) and 3.13. Resolve for the
# floor, not for the image, so a developer on an older interpreter is not locked out.
#
#   uv pip compile requirements.in --python-version 3.10 -o requirements.txt
#
# or, with pip-tools instead of uv:
#
#   pip-compile requirements.in --python-version 3.10 -o requirements.txt

